      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. UNDP in partnership with te Ministry of Energy and Mineral Resources through the Accelerating Clean Energy Access to Reduce Inequality (ACCESS) project funded by KOICA, has supported the poor and most vulnerable communities to have equitable and sustainable access to essential services for improving their livelihodd in 23 villages in 4 (four) provinces in Indonesia (East Nusa Tenggara, West Sulawesi, South-East Sulawesi, and Central Kalimantan provinces) and 25 villages in three municipalities of Timor-Leste (Municipality of Dili (Atauro), Bobonaro and Manatuto) through technical support, evidence-based policy advice,knowledge management, capacity building and partnerships. In 2022, the notable achievements are as follows:
a. Built capacity of 50 local operators from Indonesia (46% women) and 30 local operators from Timor-Leste (26% women) to learn the operations of renewable energy infrastructures.
b. Procurement and distribution of 992 solar home systems to 25 villages, benefiting 4,541 people (44% women).
c. Establishment of 21 Village Owned Enterprises (covering 23 ACCESS target locations) that will manage the built renewable energy infrastructures. 
d. 21 Village regulations on electricity tariff issued by local governments.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
